</ul>
<p>Enroll now and start learning at your pace. We have classroom sessions (Bengaluru, Noida, and Gurgaon), self-paced learning (online) and bootcamps.</p>
<h2><strong>Top Sectors Hiring Data Scientists in Hyderabad (and Why They Are Booming)</strong></h2>
<p>Hyderabad’s data science hiring is not limited to IT services. The city’s economy spans pharma, banking, semiconductors, and aerospace. Each sector uses data scientists differently. Here is what you can expect.</p>
<p><img src="https://tumfgdyurswklrzsnevv.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/uploads/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-13-at-11.41.25-AM.png" alt="data scientist jobs sectors"></p>
<h3><strong>IT Services and GCCs</strong></h3>
<p>IT services account for roughly 63% of data scientist job postings in Hyderabad on Naukri. Companies like Microsoft, Google, Amazon, and Salesforce operate large development and analytics centres in HITEC City and Raheja Mindspace. In these roles, you will work on product analytics, recommendation systems, and ML engineering. Many GCCs have moved beyond support functions into global product ownership where you build models that serve millions of users worldwide.</p>
<h3><strong>Healthcare and Life Sciences</strong></h3>
<p>This sector represents about 8.6% of postings. Hyderabad is India’s pharmaceutical capital, anchored by Genome Valley. Companies like Novartis, Sanofi, Dr. Reddy’s, and Eli Lilly run R&#x26;D centres here. As a data scientist in this sector, you will work on clinical data analysis, drug discovery modelling, and bioinformatics. The convergence of pharma infrastructure and data science talent has made Hyderabad uniquely positioned for these roles.</p>
<h3><strong>Banking, Financial Services, and Insurance (BFSI)</strong></h3>
<p>Although, BFSI accounts for about 5.4% of listings, these roles tend to pay well. Companies like JP Morgan Chase, HSBC, Wells Fargo, and MetLife all run analytics centres here. You get to work on risk modelling, fraud detection, regulatory tech, and customer analytics. Add to this, Hyderabad’s deep BFSI talent pool is another reason why global banks keep expanding here. This means, the future holds more job scope in this city. </p>
<h3><strong>Emerging Sectors</strong></h3>
<p>Semiconductors (Qualcomm, AMD, Intel), aerospace (Boeing), and automotive (Bosch, Hyundai, ZF) are few of the growing employers. In these roles, you apply data science to yield analysis, simulation modelling, and embedded systems optimization. These sectors are smaller in volume but often pay premium salaries for niche skills.</p>
